    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:entropy_horizon",
      "title": "Entropy Horizon",
      "text": "A ring of event-horizon casing that runs a universe forward to its end: stars burn out, protons decay, black holes evaporate, and the horizon glows at its own faint temperature over what is left.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 5$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "This controller is too complex for a crafting grid. Build it on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Runs matter forward to the end of time: $(item)Heat Death Embers$(), $(fluid)Dark Era Haze$(), $(item)De Sitter Horizon Shards$(), $(item)Heat Death Remnants$() and, given long enough, a $(item)Boltzmann Fluctuation$()."
    },
